														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2733070">
									

<p>Eh, no vote.</p>
<p>Going through the history of the seven sisters mentioned in 231's documentation certainly is a type of history, but the contest calls for historically significant events and figures to be central to the narrative, so I'm not really sure this works as a hiscon entry.</p>
<p>That aside, I find myself largely agreeing with psul. The tale itself doesn't really tread new ground with respect to 231 or the Administrator, and doesn't really make me feel anything for the character of Dr. Seidelman as well.</p>
<p>Its a well written tale. Its just not for me.</p>

							</div>

								
					
